  <section id="sk-inside" class="sk-section"><div class="sk-wrap"><div class="sk-section-heading"><div><p class="sk-eyebrow">01 / Working files, ready to edit</p><h2>See the files<br>before you download.</h2></div><p>One workbook holds four sheets. The PDF explains the workflow. The CSV gives you a plain call log when that is all you need.</p></div><div class="sk-file-grid">
    <article><span class="sk-file-number">01</span><div><h3>Campaign Brief</h3><p>Define your offer, target companies, buyer roles, evidence, exclusions and meeting standard. Agree how a useful opportunity reaches sales.</p><span class="sk-file-detail">9 fields to complete</span></div></article>
    <article><span class="sk-file-number">02</span><div><h3>Script Worksheet</h3><p>Draft the opening, relevance question, discovery, objection response and meeting request. Keep room for what the buyer actually says.</p><span class="sk-file-detail">8 conversation prompts</span></div></article>
    <article><span class="sk-file-number">03</span><div><h3>Call Tracker</h3><p>Record each attempt, outcome, next action, due date and owner. Outcome dropdowns and summary counts cover 200 prepared rows.</p><span class="sk-file-detail">11 columns / 7 outcome choices</span></div></article>
    <article><span class="sk-file-number">04</span><div><h3>Worked Example</h3><p>See a fictional ERP campaign for finance buyers. Follow the completed fields from the buyer and offer through to the sales handoff.</p><span class="sk-file-detail">Illustrative example included</span></div></article>
  </div><div class="sk-download-bar"><div><strong>Choose your format.</strong><p>The ZIP includes all three files and a short readme.</p></div><div class="sk-download-links"><a href="{{ downloadBase }}.xlsx" download data-kit-download>Excel workbook ↓</a><a href="{{ downloadBase }}.pdf" download data-kit-download>PDF guide ↓</a><a href="/assets/downloads/CallTeam-Cold-Call-Tracker.csv" download data-kit-download>CSV tracker ↓</a></div></div></div></section>

  <section id="sk-example" class="sk-section sk-paper"><div class="sk-wrap"><div class="sk-section-heading"><div><p class="sk-eyebrow">02 / A completed example</p><h2>Start with a buyer.<br>Give the call a purpose.</h2></div><p>This fictional example uses an ERP provider speaking with CFOs at wholesale distributors. It shows how to complete the documents.</p></div><div class="sk-example-grid"><figure class="sk-sheet-preview"><img src="/assets/images/cold-calling-starter-kit-preview.png" width="1383" height="854" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Completed buyer, offer and opening fields in the workbook’s fictional ERP campaign example."><figcaption>Inside the workbook / Worked Example sheet</figcaption></figure><div class="sk-example-copy"><dl><div><dt>Offer</dt><dd>{{ kit.example.offer }}</dd></div><div><dt>Question to investigate</dt><dd>{{ kit.example.hypothesis }}</dd></div></dl><p class="sk-label">An opening to adapt</p><blockquote>“{{ kit.example.opening }}”</blockquote><p class="sk-example-question"><strong>Explore the answer:</strong> {{ kit.example.question }}</p><p class="sk-small">Approve the offer statement before use. The caller checks the situation and records what the buyer confirms.</p></div></div><div class="sk-handoff"><strong>Give the next conversation a clear brief.</strong><p>{{ kit.example.handoff }}</p></div></div></section>

  <section id="sk-use" class="sk-section"><div class="sk-wrap"><div class="sk-section-heading"><div><p class="sk-eyebrow">03 / From download to daily use</p><h2>Put the kit to work<br>with your team.</h2></div><p>Complete the brief first. Use the worksheet to prepare and practise, then keep the tracker current as the campaign runs.</p></div><ol class="sk-use-list"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Set the campaign.</h3><p>Agree the market, buyer, offer and meeting standard. Use the <a href="/b2b-outbound-campaign-planner/">Campaign Preview</a> to explore a starting approach for your market.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Prepare your opening.</h3><p>Choose a relevant script and complete the worksheet. The <a href="/cold-call-script-checker/">Script Checker</a> can help you review its wording before practice.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Record the next action.</h3><p>Log each call attempt with the same Contact ID for repeat calls. Capture the outcome, callback date and owner. Stop the sequence when the contact asks you to.</p></div></li></ol><aside class="sk-economics"><div><p class="sk-label">Considering a managed campaign?</p><h3>Work through the economics too.</h3><p>Use your own campaign cost, conversion and customer-value assumptions to explore the potential return.</p></div><a class="sk-button" href="/b2b-lead-generation-roi-calculator/">Calculate Your Campaign ROI <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></aside></div></section>

  <section id="sk-scripts" class="sk-section sk-paper"><div class="sk-wrap"><div class="sk-section-heading"><div><p class="sk-eyebrow">04 / Choose a closer starting point</p><h2>Bring your market<br>into the worksheet.</h2></div><p>These three paths show how the kit connects to our existing resources. Use the full library for other offers, buyers and industries.</p></div><div class="sk-path-grid">{% for item in kit.paths %}<article><p class="sk-label">{{ item.market }}</p><h3>{{ item.title }}</h3><p>{{ item.text }}</p><div class="sk-path-links"><a href="{{ item.script }}">Open the script <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="{{ item.guide }}">Read the playbook <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></article>{% endfor %}</div><a class="sk-text-link" href="/resources/cold-call-scripts/">Browse all 100 B2B cold calling scripts <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>

  <section id="sk-proof" class="sk-section sk-dark"><div class="sk-wrap sk-proof-grid"><div><p class="sk-eyebrow">05 / The team behind the resources</p><h2>See the campaign work<br>behind CallTeam.</h2><p class="sk-body-lead">CallTeam runs human-led B2B calling and appointment-setting campaigns, from prospect research and follow-up to qualification and sales handoff.</p><p>Our published FinTech case study explains how a payments campaign connected a focused market, relevant conversations and a product-demo handoff. It reported 15 qualified demos in 90 days and three closed deals.</p><a class="sk-text-link" href="/case-studies/fintech-payment-platform-appointment-setting/">Read the full campaign case study <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><aside class="sk-proof-card"><p class="sk-label">When you want execution support</p><h3>Put a team<br>behind the plan.</h3><p>We can build or refine the list, prepare the message, make the calls, manage follow-up and qualify the next conversation.</p><a class="sk-button sk-button-solid" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discuss Your Calling Campaign <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="sk-text-link" href="/services/b2b-appointment-setting/">Explore appointment-setting services <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></aside></div></section>

